    "created_at": "2023-03-22T08:31:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-22T08:31:13Z",
    "body": "> We might also want to include compression parameters as part of the `format`, but I can't think of any parameters that wouldn't be better placed in a second \"option bag\" argument to the constructor.\r\n\r\nAgreed, codecs have string parameters but I don't think that's a thing for compressions.\r\n\r\n>The W3C design principles' recommendation is to just [stick with strings](https://www.w3.org/TR/design-principles/#string-constants).\r\n\r\nIt seems it's talking about C++ enums as IDL enums are still strings 🤔",
